{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-01 S2 — design grounding evidence (moved here to keep the description within the plan-review admission limit; see the Approach/Scope in the description).\n\n## `ceil(x/2)` request-budget census (full sweep of build_usage_limits)\n- `completion_banking.iteration_limit_for(B)` (line 279) returns `2*B` — the exact inverse of the base `req_limit = ceil(eff_max_iter/2)` that `build_usage_limits` RETURNS.\n- `completion_banking.plan_recovery_pool` (line 243) independently applies `ceil(floor/2)` to the verify-step floor — same `ceil(x/2)` SHAPE on a different input, so it must not be conflated with the request-budget formula.\n- `usage_log.py` / `runner.py` only RECEIVE the built `UsageLimits.request_limit` as an argument; they are NOT formula consumers.\n- Invariant preserved: `build_usage_limits` keeps RETURNING the bare base `req_limit` (telemetry + banking inverse), and the output-retry allowance is an addend ONLY inside the constructed `UsageLimits.request_limit`. The source-census test pins BOTH encodings: returned `req_limit == ceil(eff_max_iter/2)` AND `UsageLimits.request_limit == base + allowance`.\n- Impacted existing seam tests (both pin the CONSTRUCTED request_limit, so both move base→base+allowance): `test_settings_builders_seam.py:80` and `test_llm_failure_matrix.py::test_runner_computes_derived_usage_limits:341`.\n\n## pydantic-ai shared-counter mechanism (verified in source + empirically, pydantic-ai 1.107.2)\n- A single per-run counter `_agent_graph.GraphAgentState.output_retries_used` (line 127) is incremented by `consume_output_retry(max_output_retries)` (line 162), which raises `UnexpectedModelBehavior(\"Exceeded maximum output retries (N)\")` when exceeded (lines 176-178).\n- BOTH a capability-hook `ModelRetry` (via `_build_retry_node`, line 1036) AND a `TextOutput`-validator `ModelRetry` decrement this SAME counter, bounded by `retries={\"output\": N}`.\n- Spike proof: error-retry (guard) + invalid-json-retry (output fn) with R=1 exhausts after 2 calls; R=2 succeeds after 3 calls. The plan pins this BEHAVIORALLY (success at exactly N, abort at N-1) via the limit-matrix oracle rather than citing private internals (the reviewer sandbox cannot verify private symbols).\n\n## Wire-projection fit rule grounding (public fields only)\n- Each `ModelResponse` carries a public `.usage` (`RequestUsage` with `input_tokens`/`output_tokens`) — VERIFIED public field.\n- `model_classes.own_window_tokens(model)` (model_classes.py:69) is the established single source of model context-window knowledge (substring match against `MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER`; unknown -> ladder minimum, conservative per bug 48b3). This is the \"window\" the fit rule references — it EXISTS.\n- Fit rule uses only public fields + this existing helper — no private internals.\n\n## structured.py classification authority (must NOT be mutated)\n- `_UNRETRYABLE_STOP_REASONS = frozenset({refusal, max_tokens, length, content_filter})` (line 632).\n- `check_stop_reason(stop_reason)` (line 635) inspects ONLY the normalized finish_reason and RAISES (truncation/refusal -> `UnretryableOutputError`; `error` -> retryable `StructuredOutputError`).\n- `check_response(response)` (line 651) does TWO layers: finish_reason via check_stop_reason PLUS the raw `provider_details['finish_reason']`/`'refusal'` key (the #5221 defense). Neither RETURNS a reason — both only RAISE, which is why the S2 guard does its own read-only two-layer read for the truncation subset before delegating.\n- `OUTPUT_RETRIES = 2` is the default allowance N."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786937603649858001,"uuid":"d574300d-467a-4c66-a9d3-497e7eb824e1"}